-- Adds account-deletion steps to the Privacy Policy and the Help article,
-- including a way to request deletion by email without the app. Google Play
-- requires a public web page explaining how to delete an account; the Play
-- Console deletion URL is /privacy-policy#how-to-delete-your-meetifyy-account
-- (the heading id is derived from the heading text by LegalDocumentPage).
--
-- At the owner's explicit request the Privacy Policy stays VERSION 1, with its
-- effective, created, updated and published dates all unchanged at
-- 27 August 2026. So this edits the existing version-1 row in place instead of
-- publishing a version 2, and sets no timestamp. The text is a verbatim copy of
-- PRIVACY_POLICY in frontend/src/features/info/pages/legalDocuments.js.
-- requiresAcknowledgement is untouched, so nobody is put behind the consent gate.
--
-- The Help article is updated by slug. If an admin edited it in the portal,
-- this replaces that edit with the text below.
-- Plain UPDATEs: no CONCURRENTLY, no schema-qualified names.
UPDATE "LegalDocumentVersion"
SET "content" = $legal$<p>This policy explains how Meetifyy collects, uses, discloses and retains personal information through the Meetifyy website, mobile app and support channels. In this policy, “we”, “us” and “our” refer to Meetifyy.</p><h2>Information we handle and why</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Category</th><th>Information and purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Account and profile</td><td>We use your name, username, email address and sign-in details to create and administer your account. We use date of birth to assess age eligibility when it is provided. We process the profile information you supply, such as gender, biography, interests, location, and profile and cover images, to maintain your profile and support discovery and connections. Our authentication provider handles the password you enter. We also record acknowledgements of applicable policies.</td></tr><tr><td>Campus affiliation</td><td>If you apply for Campus access, we use your college email address, college and verification details to confirm your affiliation and determine access. We process academic information you provide, such as your course, branch or year of study. Your college email can also indicate your joining year. When you ask us to add a college, we use the college and contact details you submit to handle the request.</td></tr><tr><td>Account verification</td><td>If you request account verification, we collect the live selfie or live photograph of an identity document you submit, together with submission and decision details. Some older versions may request both images. A document photo may show your name, date of birth, photo, address or identification number, depending on the document you use. We use this material to review eligibility for features that require account verification and to handle related reviews. Verification images are handled privately and are unavailable to other members.</td></tr><tr><td>Content and activity</td><td>We process the posts, comments, polls, links, images and videos you submit, your Confessions handle and posts, and your interactions such as searches, saves, reactions, votes, community membership and event or Crew participation. We use this information to operate the features you choose, surface relevant content and activities, and apply audience rules.</td></tr><tr><td>Messages</td><td>We process direct and group messages, including voice notes and other attachments, and details such as participants and timestamps. We use this information to deliver conversations and make history available to participants. Authorised personnel may review reported messages to investigate abuse, enforce our rules or address a legal obligation.</td></tr><tr><td>Instant Match</td><td>We process your matching preferences and any campus area you select to suggest compatible matches. If you choose to share your precise device location and grant permission, we process that location to help find nearby matches. You can use the location controls in your device or browser to change this permission.</td></tr><tr><td>Support, safety and complaints</td><td>We collect what you or others send us in support requests, reports, appeals and complaints, including contact details, descriptions, links, attachments and records about the report. We use it to respond, assess safety issues, enforce rules and comply with legal duties.</td></tr><tr><td>Service and device activity</td><td>We process information such as IP address, browser or operating system, app or device details, connection and activity timestamps, and error and performance information. We use this information to manage sessions and devices, help protect accounts, measure service performance and investigate problems.</td></tr><tr><td>Notifications and communications</td><td>If you enable push notifications, we process subscription or device delivery information and the data needed to send and manage notifications. We also use contact details to send verification codes, account and security messages, support replies, and policy notices.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Some information about you comes from other people. This can include information they include in messages, posts, mentions, reports or support requests. For device storage and website measurement, see the <a href="/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.</p><h2>Who can receive information</h2><ul><li><strong>Other people using Meetifyy.</strong> Profile details and content are visible according to the feature, applicable audience and your settings. Campus, community, group and conversation access may depend on affiliation or membership. Recipients can keep, copy or forward what you share with them. Where public sharing is available, people outside Meetifyy may see previews of eligible public posts.</li><li><strong>Confessions.</strong> Other members see the handle used for Confessions instead of the associated profile name. Meetifyy can link that handle to the account for authorised moderation and safety purposes and to comply with lawful requests. Details in a confession can identify you or someone else.</li><li><strong>Service providers.</strong> Providers that help us with sign-in, hosting and media storage, email and push delivery, website measurement and diagnostics receive information relevant to the service they provide. For example, an email delivery provider receives the recipient address and the message to deliver.</li><li><strong>External content and websites.</strong> Some previews or images displayed on Meetifyy involve requests to external services. Those requests may disclose the URL needed to retrieve the content, or connection information such as your IP address when your device makes the request. When you follow an external link, the destination handles information under its own privacy terms.</li><li><strong>Authorities and other recipients required by law.</strong> We may provide relevant information to courts, public authorities or other recipients when legally required or otherwise permitted by applicable law in connection with safety, fraud, legal claims or enforcement.</li></ul><h2>Retention and account deletion</h2><p>We keep account information and user content to operate accounts and provide the features described above. The period depends on the category of information, the service it supports, what remains in a shared space, and any applicable retention duty.</p><h2>How to delete your Meetifyy account</h2><p>In the Meetifyy app or on the website, open <strong>Settings</strong>, select <strong>Privacy &amp; Security</strong>, then <strong>Delete Account</strong>, and confirm the request with the code sent to your email. Your account enters a 30-day recovery window during which you can cancel deletion through the account recovery prompt. After the window closes, the account becomes eligible for permanent deletion.</p><p>If you cannot sign in or no longer have the app, email <a href="mailto:support@meetifyy.app">support@meetifyy.app</a> from the email address registered to your account, with the subject “Delete my account” and your username. We may ask you to confirm the request before we act on it. Deletion then follows the same process described in this section. You can also find these steps in <a href="/help-and-support?q=delete%20account">Help &amp; Support</a>.</p><p>When account deletion is processed, the account profile is removed from normal member access and the deletion process removes the posts, Confessions and Crew activities you created. Some information can remain:</p><ul><li>Other participants may still see messages and discussion contributions in their shared history under “Deleted User”. The text or files they have can contain information that identifies you.</li><li>Communities with other members may continue under another owner. Published Campus events may remain available.</li><li>Meetifyy may keep support and moderation records for their applicable retention period. Their original text or attachments can still contain personal information.</li><li>People may keep copies of information they previously received or saved. A legal hold or other legal duty may require Meetifyy to preserve certain records.</li></ul><p>Under the Information Technology (Intermediary Guidelines and Digital Media Ethics Code) Rules, 2021, intermediaries must retain registration information for 180 days following cancellation or withdrawal of registration. The Rules also require preservation of specified removed or disabled material and associated records for 180 days, or longer when a lawfully authorised court or agency requires it. <a href="https://www.meity.gov.in/static/uploads/2026/02/550681ab908f8afb135b0ad42816a1c9.pdf">Intermediary Rules 3(1)(g) and (h)</a></p><h2>Your choices and requests</h2><p>You can review and update available profile and account fields in Settings. Use <strong>Visibility</strong> to manage available visibility options and <strong>Notifications</strong> to manage notification preferences. You can remove a verified college email in <strong>Email</strong>. Removing it ends access to the Campus features that depend on that affiliation. You can also change location, camera, microphone and notification permissions in your browser or device. Changing a permission affects future access through that permission.</p><p>You may contact us to request review of personal information you provided, correction of inaccurate or incomplete information, or deletion, subject to applicable law. You can decline to supply information. When processing depends on your consent, you can withdraw it in writing using the privacy contact below. Declining or withdrawing can affect features that require the information. For example, features that require account verification depend on completing a verification check. We may ask for information reasonably needed to verify your identity or your authority to act for someone else.</p><h2>Security and age eligibility</h2><p>We use reasonable safeguards appropriate to the information we handle, including limiting access to private verification materials. If you suspect unauthorised access to your account, contact <a href="mailto:support@meetifyy.app">Meetifyy Support</a>.</p><p>Meetifyy is for people aged 18 or older. If you believe someone under 18 has registered or provided personal information, contact <a href="mailto:support@meetifyy.app">Meetifyy Support</a> so we can assess the report and take appropriate action.</p><h2>Privacy contact and changes to this policy</h2><p>For privacy requests or complaints, contact <a href="mailto:support@meetifyy.app">Meetifyy Support</a>. We will publish the effective date of any revised policy and provide notice or seek consent where applicable law requires it.</p>$legal$
WHERE "documentType" = 'PRIVACY_POLICY' AND "versionNumber" = 1;

UPDATE "HelpArticle"
SET "body" = $help$<p>Go to <strong>Settings</strong>, then <strong>Privacy &amp; Security</strong>, and choose <strong>Delete Account</strong> at the bottom. We email you a code to confirm it is really you.</p>
<p>Your account is then scheduled for deletion. <strong>For 30 days you can change your mind:</strong> sign in, choose <strong>Recover my account</strong> and enter the code we email you. After 30 days your profile, posts and messages are permanently erased.</p>
<p><strong>Can't sign in, or no longer have the app?</strong> Email <a href="mailto:support@meetifyy.app">support@meetifyy.app</a> from the email address on your account, with the subject “Delete my account” and your username. We may ask you to confirm before we delete it.</p>
<p>Some records are kept where we must keep them, for example safety reports made about an account, so a report cannot be erased by deleting the account it is about. The <a href="/privacy-policy#how-to-delete-your-meetifyy-account">Privacy Policy</a> lists what is removed and what may remain.</p>
<p>Want a break rather than leaving? Turn on <strong>Private Profile</strong> under Settings, Visibility instead.</p>$help$,
    "keywords" = ARRAY['delete account','close account','remove account','deactivate','erase data','recover account','30 days','delete my data','email']::TEXT[]
WHERE "slug" = 'how-do-i-delete-my-account';
